He he he he he!

269
00:13:10,797 --> 00:13:11,797
He he he!

270
00:13:11,797 --> 00:13:12,797
Slow, slow beam!

271
00:13:12,797 --> 00:13:13,797
Slow, slow beam!

272
00:13:13,797 --> 00:13:16,797
And the winner is the Cutie Wagon!

273
00:13:16,797 --> 00:13:19,797
The hero of the first round of the Davy Back Fight is our very own idol, Porcha!

274
00:13:19,797 --> 00:13:20,797
Way to go!

275
00:13:20,797 --> 00:13:21,797
Thank you! Thanks everyone!

276
00:13:21,797 --> 00:13:22,797
You're the greatest, Porcha!

277
00:13:22,797 --> 00:13:23,797
It's only natural, I won!

278
00:13:23,797 --> 00:13:24,797
Looks like we're about to get a new crew member!

279
00:13:24,797 --> 00:13:27,797
There's nobody that can beat the Foxy Pirates! We always win!

280
00:13:57,797 --> 00:14:01,797
Now it's time for you guys to play up! We're taking one of your crew!

281
00:14:02,797 --> 00:14:04,797
You guys hurt? Is everybody okay? Robin?

282
00:14:04,797 --> 00:14:06,797
Yes. We're alright.

283
00:14:06,797 --> 00:14:08,797
What the heck happened out there?

284
00:14:08,797 --> 00:14:10,797
I'd like to know the same thing!

285
00:14:10,797 --> 00:14:13,797
We'd all like to know what happened! Did we really lose somehow?

286
00:14:13,797 --> 00:14:17,797
You looked like you were gonna win, but then you suddenly slowed down and they passed you!

287
00:14:17,797 --> 00:14:25,797
There's nothing strange about that! It was caused by slow-mo photon!

288
00:14:25,797 --> 00:14:28,797
Hey, what did you do to Nami's team, you smug bastard?

289
00:14:28,797 --> 00:14:30,797
What's a slow-mo photon?

290
00:14:30,797 --> 00:14:34,797
They are particles unlike any others known to modern science!

291
00:14:34,797 --> 00:14:38,797
Whatever this light touches, be it an animal, a liquid, a solid, or even a gas,

292
00:14:38,797 --> 00:14:44,797
will lose a fixed amount of its velocity, while simultaneously retaining all its other energy!

293
00:14:44,797 --> 00:14:47,797
You're dumb! That makes no sense at all!

294
00:14:47,797 --> 00:14:48,797
He just mocked me!

295
00:14:48,797 --> 00:14:53,797
Oh! So are you okay? No way! Something that ridiculous is just...

296
00:14:53,797 --> 00:14:55,797
Impossible? Is that what you're thinking?

297
00:14:55,797 --> 00:15:01,797
Surely you know that such a naive, childish claim has no merit out here on these waters!

298
00:15:01,797 --> 00:15:04,797
Everything they touch slows down, that's the power of slow-mo photons!

299
00:15:04,797 --> 00:15:07,797
Now that makes sense! Why didn't you say so before?

300
00:15:07,797 --> 00:15:13,797
After I ate the slow, slow fruit, I became a slow-motion man, capable of producing these particles from my body!

301
00:15:13,797 --> 00:15:15,797
Observe!

302
00:15:18,797 --> 00:15:20,797
A floating cannonball!

303
00:15:20,797 --> 00:15:22,797
The slow, slow beam!

304
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:30,797
The effect lasts approximately 30 seconds, after which the object will regain its original speed as if nothing had ever happened!

305
00:15:30,797 --> 00:15:35,797
Can't believe your eyes I take it, this...

306
00:15:35,797 --> 00:15:38,797
Oh no!

307
00:15:38,797 --> 00:15:42,797
I get it! So that's why we didn't win the race!

308
00:15:42,797 --> 00:15:46,797
It also explains why they're so overly confident about these games!

309
00:15:46,797 --> 00:15:48,797
What a joke of a devil fruit power!

310
00:15:48,797 --> 00:15:52,797
It doesn't matter! You guys lost! You know all the rules and you agree to all the terms!

311
00:15:52,797 --> 00:15:56,797
The donut race is over! And we are the winners!

312
00:15:57,797 --> 00:15:59,797
Aw, too bad for you guys!

313
00:15:59,797 --> 00:16:04,797
That concludes round one! And now we shall commence with the awarding of the prize!

314
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:07,797
The winning captain will select a member of the opposing crew!

315
00:16:07,797 --> 00:16:21,797
My first selection is none other than...

316
00:16:21,797 --> 00:16:25,797
You! The Doctor! Tony Tony Chopper!

317
00:16:26,797 --> 00:16:28,797
Bring him to me at once!

318
00:16:28,797 --> 00:16:29,797
No! No! Stop it!

319
00:16:29,797 --> 00:16:30,797
Oh no! Chopper!

320
00:16:31,797 --> 00:16:35,797
Such a rare creature! You're even softer than I imagined you'd be!

321
00:16:36,797 --> 00:16:39,797
Oh, boss me! I hold him too!

322
00:16:40,797 --> 00:16:42,797
You're so damn cute! And he's ours now!

323
00:16:45,797 --> 00:16:46,797
Chopper!

324
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:51,797
So that creep had his eyes set on Chopper, huh?

325
00:16:51,797 --> 00:16:54,797
Well, I suppose that he is among the rarest of rare animals.

326
00:16:54,797 --> 00:16:56,797
Or maybe he collects cute things?

327
00:16:56,797 --> 00:16:58,797
You know, I wouldn't rule out a fur fetish.

328
00:16:58,797 --> 00:17:03,797
Why does it even matter? Focus, people! That freak over there just took our friend!

329
00:17:03,797 --> 00:17:04,797
You guys!

330
00:17:06,797 --> 00:17:10,797
Alright, Doctor Chopper. Enough of all that. You're one of my crew now.

331
00:17:10,797 --> 00:17:15,797
You need to pledge your loyalty to me. And you can start by putting on this mask.

332
00:17:15,797 --> 00:17:18,797
You guys!

333
00:17:19,797 --> 00:17:22,797
I'm so sorry that we lost Chopper! We did our best!

334
00:17:22,797 --> 00:17:23,797
Farewell!

335
00:17:24,797 --> 00:17:27,797
He is truly a rarity!

336
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:31,797
Our Mario Talking Reindeer! He's so amazing!

337
00:17:32,797 --> 00:17:34,797
We're gonna get along great! Here!

338
00:17:35,797 --> 00:17:36,797
Welcome aboard!

339
00:17:40,797 --> 00:17:41,797
You guys!

340
00:17:41,797 --> 00:17:42,797
Listen!

341
00:17:43,797 --> 00:17:46,797
I only went out to sea because of you!

342
00:17:47,797 --> 00:17:48,797
I won't!

343
00:17:49,797 --> 00:17:50,797
No! I refuse!

344
00:17:51,797 --> 00:17:53,797
Luffy! You invited me!

345
00:17:53,797 --> 00:17:55,797
I sent sail to be one of the Straw Hats!

346
00:17:56,797 --> 00:17:57,797
I won't go with them!

347
00:17:58,797 --> 00:17:59,797
Please!

348
00:17:59,797 --> 00:18:00,797
No!

349
00:18:00,797 --> 00:18:02,797
I am the ship's doctor of the Straw Hat Pirates!

350
00:18:03,797 --> 00:18:04,797
Tony Tony Chopper!

351
00:18:04,797 --> 00:18:05,797
I won't go!

352
00:18:07,797 --> 00:18:08,797
I won't go!

353
00:18:09,797 --> 00:18:12,797
Quit your belly aching, Chopper!

354
00:18:13,797 --> 00:18:14,797
It's disgraceful!

355
00:18:15,797 --> 00:18:16,797
Uh... Zoro?

356
00:18:17,797 --> 00:18:18,797
You made the choice to set sail as a pirate.

357
00:18:19,797 --> 00:18:20,797
Only you!

358
00:18:21,797 --> 00:18:23,797
And now you have to live with the consequences of that decision.

359
00:18:24,797 --> 00:18:25,797
We agreed to the terms of this game.

360
00:18:26,797 --> 00:18:28,797
You, Usopp, and everyone else did the best they could.

361
00:18:29,797 --> 00:18:33,797
Not one pirate worth his salt is gonna sympathize with those tears.

362
00:18:34,797 --> 00:18:38,797
A man would suck it up and quietly watch the rest of this game.

363
00:18:39,797 --> 00:18:40,797
What's wrong with you?

364
00:18:41,797 --> 00:18:43,797
Don't you know how he must be feeling?

365
00:18:44,797 --> 00:18:49,797
Boil me or cook me alive!

366
00:18:50,797 --> 00:18:52,797
Give me your worst, you bastards!

367
00:18:53,797 --> 00:18:54,797
Chopper?

368
00:18:55,797 --> 00:18:56,797
Atta boy.

369
00:18:57,797 --> 00:18:58,797
Whoa! That swordsman is totally awesome!

370
00:18:59,797 --> 00:19:00,797
All right! You teach him a lesson, Zoro!

371
00:19:01,797 --> 00:19:02,797
Yeah! Get Chopper back!

372
00:19:03,797 --> 00:19:04,797
Hey, boss! Let's take him next!

373
00:19:05,797 --> 00:19:06,797
That reindeer's not guns!

374
00:19:07,797 --> 00:19:08,797
Let's get the second event started.

375
00:19:09,797 --> 00:19:10,797
So inspirational, I can't stop crying!

376
00:19:10,797 --> 00:19:13,797
Yeah, we still have two rounds left of this.

377
00:19:14,797 --> 00:19:17,797
There's no way we're letting these jerks take our emergency food supply.

378
00:19:18,797 --> 00:19:19,797
Sachi!

379
00:19:19,797 --> 00:19:20,797
We're counting on you!

380
00:19:20,797 --> 00:19:24,797
The exchange is complete and the excitement explodes as the daily backbite enters round two!

381
00:19:25,797 --> 00:19:28,797
Hey, wasn't Chopper supposed to be in the second round? How can he compete if they took him?

382
00:19:29,797 --> 00:19:30,797
Good point.

383
00:19:31,797 --> 00:19:32,797
That's one of the most thrilling parts of the game!

384
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:35,797
Remember the rules, you cannot change your team's roster.

385
00:19:36,797 --> 00:19:37,797
No replacements allowed!

386
00:19:37,797 --> 00:19:41,797
In other words, only the remaining two contestants can participate in round two's game!

387
00:19:42,797 --> 00:19:44,797
The groggy ring! This gives the foxy team an artly advantage!

388
00:19:45,797 --> 00:19:46,797
What? That's not fair!

389
00:19:46,797 --> 00:19:47,797
Actually, you could sit this one out, too.

390
00:19:48,797 --> 00:19:51,797
Nah, but feel free to do the same thing, you loser.

391
00:19:52,797 --> 00:19:54,797
It's hard to believe that they're gonna work together as a team.

392
00:19:55,797 --> 00:19:56,797
What was that?

393
00:19:57,797 --> 00:19:58,797
Knock it off!

394
00:19:58,797 --> 00:19:59,797
And the rules of the groggy ring!

395
00:19:59,797 --> 00:20:01,797
We have a playing field, and we have two goals!

396
00:20:02,797 --> 00:20:03,797
Knock the ball into the goal, and you win!

397
00:20:04,797 --> 00:20:06,797
However, the ball isn't actually a ball!

398
00:20:06,797 --> 00:20:07,797
The balls are people!

399
00:20:08,797 --> 00:20:10,797
Both teams must select someone to be the ball!

400
00:20:11,797 --> 00:20:12,797
Make your selection!

401
00:20:13,797 --> 00:20:15,797
You heard him! Which one of you two guys is gonna be the ball?

402
00:20:16,797 --> 00:20:17,797
Ball marker!

403
00:20:17,797 --> 00:20:21,797
Who said you get to pick? You're the ball, you moss-headed bastard!

404
00:20:22,797 --> 00:20:25,797
Oh, there it is! Their entrance theme song!

405
00:20:26,797 --> 00:20:29,797
It's time to welcome back the undisputed elites of the groggy ring!

406
00:20:30,797 --> 00:20:32,797
They are undefeated! Unbeatable!

407
00:20:33,797 --> 00:20:34,797
Unstammable!

408
00:20:35,797 --> 00:20:36,797
Yeah! Crush'em!

409
00:20:36,797 --> 00:20:39,797
Push-up! The famous groggy monsters have taken the field!

410
00:20:40,797 --> 00:20:42,797
Behold, the kings of the ring!

411
00:20:45,797 --> 00:20:48,797
First up is Full Dash Hamburg!

412
00:20:49,797 --> 00:20:51,797
Following behind is Taco Machine Pickles!

413
00:20:52,797 --> 00:20:56,797
And last but not least, the half-giant, half-fish-man himself!

414
00:20:57,797 --> 00:20:59,797
Big Pan Luatang!

415
00:21:00,797 --> 00:21:02,797
This is literally a monstrous march!

416
00:21:02,797 --> 00:21:04,797
Yeah! Yeah!

417
00:21:09,797 --> 00:21:10,797
What is that?

418
00:21:11,797 --> 00:21:13,797
That fish-man is ginormous!

419
00:21:14,797 --> 00:21:16,797
Oh crap! He's the one wearing the ball marker!

420
00:21:17,797 --> 00:21:18,797
Fish-fish!

421
00:21:19,797 --> 00:21:20,797
You'll never beat him!

422
00:21:25,797 --> 00:21:26,797
Disappointed?

423
00:21:28,797 --> 00:21:29,797
Not at all.

424
00:21:32,797 --> 00:21:34,797
!

425
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:11,271
On the next one piece round to shoot it into the groggy ring

